Package: DENSaftertransform
Title: Estimating Density after Logarithmic or Power Transformation of
        Data
Version: 1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Olga", "Savchuk", , "olga.y.savchuk@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Maintainer: Olga Savchuk <olga.y.savchuk@gmail.com>
Description: Functions for computing: (1) the adaptive normal plug-in(PI) density estimate for data after the logarithmic transformation; (2) the adaptive log-normal PI density estimate for data after the power transformation with an exponent ranging from zero to one; (3) the single-bandwidth PI density estimate for data after the logarithmic transformation; (4) the single-bandwidth PI density estimate for data after the power transformation; (5) the data-driven bandwidth for the single-bandwidth PI estimator for data after the logarithmic transformation; (6) the rule-of-thumb bandwidth for the single-bandwidth PI estimator for data after the power transformation. For details, see the articles: (1) Savchuk, O. (2026) (submitted). Adaptive log-normal plug-in density estimator for power transformations. (2) Savchuk, O. (2026). Density estimation for log-transformed data. Computational Statistics, 41(98) <doi:10.1007/s00180-026-01766-y>. (3) Savchuk, O., Schick A. (2013). Density estimation for power transformations. Journal of Nonparametric Statistics, 25(3), 545-559 <doi:10.1080/10485252.2013.811788>.
